      <h2>🔑 Pro Tips to Get Even Better Results</h2>

      <div class="highlight-box">
        <h3>⚡ The 5 Secrets to Perfect Prompts</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Be Specific:</strong> The more details you provide, the better Claude understands. Instead of "help me write an email," say "write a professional email asking for a meeting with the CEO about a new partnership."</li>
          <li><strong>Set Constraints:</strong> Tell Claude your limitations. "Write this in 150 words," "use simple language," "make it funny"—these constraints lead to better results.</li>
          <li><strong>Ask for Format:</strong> Don't just ask for advice. Ask for "a 5-point list," "a step-by-step guide," "a table comparing pros and cons." Format matters.</li>
          <li><strong>Iterate and Refine:</strong> The first response isn't always perfect. Ask follow-up questions, request examples, ask it to elaborate. This is where the magic happens.</li>
          <li><strong>Copy What Works:</strong> When you get a great response, save it. Use it as a template for similar requests. Over time, you build a library of killer prompts.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2>📖 How to Use These Prompts (3 Steps)</h2>

      <div class="tip-section">
        <strong>Step 1: Copy the Prompt</strong> — Find one that matches your needs and copy the exact wording.
      </div>

      <div class="tip-section">
        <strong>Step 2: Customize It</strong> — Replace generic details with your specific situation. Change "someone" to "me," adjust timeframes, add your context.
      </div>

      <div class="tip-section">
        <strong>Step 3: Ask Follow-Ups</strong> — The real magic happens here. Ask Claude to expand, simplify, give examples, or adjust the approach based on your feedback.
      </div>

